        "payload": "tree 45c65a8dc303f8ee915c832c11d79698d7993eac\nparent ed7dd7cf4e1561a97edf72eba29a67b14e28c717\nauthor FlashW <flashwayne00@gmail.com> 1790461029 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790461029 +0400\n\nkernel: don't reuse cached CheckBlock results across params\n\nCheckBlock returns early when block.fChecked is set, and the signet\nsolution is only checked inside CheckBlock. A btck_Block wraps a shared\nCBlock (btck_block_copy only adds a reference), so once a block passed\nbtck_block_check or btck_chainstate_manager_process_block under one set\nof consensus params, every later check on the same object passes,\nwhatever params or flags are used. For example, a regtest block checked\nfirst with regtest params then passes btck_block_check with mainnet\nparams, and a signet block accepted by a chainstate manager with an\nOP_TRUE challenge is also connected by a second one with an OP_RETURN\nchallenge.\n\nRun both entry points on a copy of the block without the cached\nfChecked/merkle/witness flags. The copy only shares the transaction\npointers. This also avoids writing to the caller's block from\nbtck_block_check without cs_main.",
